{"id":"h18t3","name":"Supplier Spend Trends","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>purchase_orders</b> has the columns <code>po_id</code>, <code>ordered_on</code> (date), <code>supplier</code>, <code>qty</code> and <code>unit_cost</code>. Supplier names were typed by hand: compare them after trimming spaces and converting to upper case (<code>' acme '</code> is <code>ACME</code>). Orders with <code>qty</code> &lt;= 0 are cancelled and ignored.</p>\n<p>The <b>spend</b> of a supplier in a month is the total of <code>qty * unit_cost</code>. Build a report with one row per supplier and per month, for <b>every month</b> from the supplier's first to its last order month (both included, spend 0 for months without orders). For each row compute:</p>\n<ul><li><code>spend</code>, rounded to 2 decimals;</li>\n<li><code>mom_pct</code>: <code>100 * (spend - previous month spend) / previous month spend</code>, rounded to 1 decimal, <code>NULL</code> for the first month or when the previous spend is 0;</li>\n<li><code>ma3</code>: the average spend of this month and the 2 previous months, rounded to 2 decimals, <code>NULL</code> when the supplier does not have 2 previous months in the report yet;</li>\n<li><code>yoy_pct</code>: the same as <code>mom_pct</code> but against the same month one year before, <code>NULL</code> when that month is not in the report or its spend is 0.</li></ul>\n<p>Your task is to return the columns <code>supplier</code> (clean name), <code>month</code> (first day of the month, as a date), <code>spend</code>, <code>mom_pct</code>, <code>ma3</code> and <code>yoy_pct</code>, sorted by <code>supplier</code>, then <code>month</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>purchase_orders</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>po_id</th><th>ordered_on</th><th>supplier</th><th>qty</th><th>unit_cost</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2025-01-15</td><td>acme</td><td>10</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2025-01-20</td><td> ACME </td><td>2</td><td>25</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>2025-03-02</td><td>Acme</td><td>4</td><td>25</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2025-04-30</td><td>ACME</td><td>0</td><td>99</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>2025-04-01</td><td>acme</td><td>1</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2026-01-10</td><td>ACME</td><td>5</td><td>30</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>2025-02-11</td><td>Delta</td><td>3</td><td>3.33</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>2025-03-11</td><td>delta</td><td>-3</td><td>3.33</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>supplier</th><th>month</th><th>spend</th><th>mom_pct</th><th>ma3</th><th>yoy_pct</th></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-01-01</td><td>100.0</td><td>null</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-02-01</td><td>0.0</td><td>-100.0</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-03-01</td><td>100.0</td><td>null</td><td>66.67</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-04-01</td><td>50.0</td><td>-50.0</td><td>50.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-05-01</td><td>0.0</td><td>-100.0</td><td>50.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-06-01</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td><td>16.67</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-07-01</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-08-01</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-09-01</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-10-01</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-11-01</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2025-12-01</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>ACME</td><td>2026-01-01</td><td>150.0</td><td>null</td><td>50.0</td><td>50.0</td></tr><tr><td>DELTA</td><td>2025-02-01</td><td>9.99</td><td>null</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>purchase_orders</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>supplier</code>, <code>month</code>, <code>spend</code>, <code>mom_pct</code>, <code>ma3</code>, <code>yoy_pct</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["mois manquants","generate_series","LAG 1 et LAG 12","moyenne mobile","noms à normaliser"],"minutes":25,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>purchase_orders</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 6 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>supplier</code>, <code>month</code>, <code>spend</code>, <code>mom_pct</code>, <code>ma3</code>, <code>yoy_pct</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide ; les dates s'affichent AAAA-MM-JJ.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"purchase_orders":{"columns":[["po_id","INT"],["ordered_on","DATE"],["supplier","TEXT"],["qty","INT"],["unit_cost","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[[1,"2025-01-15","acme",10,5],[2,"2025-01-20"," ACME ",2,25],[3,"2025-03-02","Acme",4,25],[4,"2025-04-30","ACME",0,99],[5,"2025-04-01","acme",1,50],[6,"2026-01-10","ACME",5,30],[7,"2025-02-11","Delta",3,3.33],[8,"2025-03-11","delta",-3,3.33]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["supplier","month","spend","mom_pct","ma3","yoy_pct"],"rows":[["ACME","2025-01-01",100.0,null,null,null],["ACME","2025-02-01",0.0,-100.0,null,null],["ACME","2025-03-01",100.0,null,66.67,null],["ACME","2025-04-01",50.0,-50.0,50.0,null],["ACME","2025-05-01",0.0,-100.0,50.0,null],["ACME","2025-06-01",0.0,null,16.67,null],["ACME","2025-07-01",0.0,null,0.0,null],["ACME","2025-08-01",0.0,null,0.0,null],["ACME","2025-09-01",0.0,null,0.0,null],["ACME","2025-10-01",0.0,null,0.0,null],["ACME","2025-11-01",0.0,null,0.0,null],["ACME","2025-12-01",0.0,null,0.0,null],["ACME","2026-01-01",150.0,null,50.0,50.0],["DELTA","2025-02-01",9.99,null,null,null]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"purchase_orders":{"columns":[["po_id","INT"],["ordered_on","DATE"],["supplier","TEXT"],["qty","INT"],["unit_cost","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[[1,"2026-05-05","zeta",1,10],[2,"2026-06-05","ZETA",1,0],[3,"2026-07-05","zeta",2,10]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["supplier","month","spend","mom_pct","ma3","yoy_pct"],"rows":[["ZETA","2026-05-01",10.0,null,null,null],["ZETA","2026-06-01",0.0,-100.0,null,null],["ZETA","2026-07-01",20.0,null,10.0,null]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}